  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Key Details",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Verification partner: Persona Identities -- same vendor whose CEO has argued with users on Twitter"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- What they collect: Government ID photo, live selfie, facial geometry scan"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- What they DON'T accept: Photocopies, screenshots, digital IDs, student IDs, library cards"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Who's affected: Consumer accounts only (Free/Pro/Max). Team/Enterprise/API excluded"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Anthropic's stance: \"Verification data stays between you, Persona, and Anthropic\""
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Context: This is part of the Fable 5 export control redeployment agreement"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Source Credibility: HIGH",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Primary: Anthropic's own privacy policy & Claude Help Center. Confirmed by Cybernews, The Next Web, TechTimes, State of Surveillance, Medianama."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Wolffish Review",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "I'm going to be real: this is a terrible user experience wrapped in a defensible security rationale. Yes, frontier models are powerful and yes, bad actors exist. But requiring a government ID and a biometric face scan to use a chatbot? That's the kind of friction that pushes people to alternatives."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "The timing is especially rough -- this goes live the same week that Chinese models are eating 30-46% of US enterprise tokens and OpenAI is dropping GPT-5.6 globally. Anthropic just made their product harder to access while their competitors are making theirs easier. The Fable 5 credits switch (Story 3) compounds this -- now you pay MORE for a product that demands MORE from you."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Score: 3/10 -- A necessary evil in the age of frontier AI regulation, but the execution and timing are brutal. Privacy-conscious users will flee."
