  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "[PRICING] Story 3: Fable 5 Goes Pay-Per-Use -- The Free Ride Is Over",
    "level": 2
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "THE STORY: As of July 8, Anthropic's flagship Claude Fable 5 model is no longer included in any subscription plan. It now requires prepaid usage credits at $10 per million input tokens and $50 per million output tokens -- double the cost of Opus 4.8 and the most expensive model Anthropic has ever priced. Subscribers who don't enable credits simply lose access."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Key Details",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Pricing: $10/M input tokens, $50/M output tokens (2x Opus 4.8, 5x Sonnet 5)"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Previously: Included in Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise for up to 50% of weekly usage"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Now: Pay-per-use credits only, managed from Settings / Usage on claude.ai"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Pro plan deadline: July 15 for remaining included credits"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- API pricing unchanged: Same rates apply directly on the API"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Context: This was always the plan -- Anthropic announced the timeline weeks ago"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Source Credibility: HIGH",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Primary: Anthropic pricing page & official announcements. Android Headlines, TechTimes, Digital Applied, CoderSera all confirm the same numbers."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Wolffish Review",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Brutal but honest: Fable 5 was never going to be free forever. The model is genuinely powerful and expensive to run. But the triple whammy -- ID verification goes live, Fable 5 goes pay-per-use, AND OpenAI drops GPT-5.6 globally -- all in the same 24 hours? That's a PR disaster dressed as a Tuesday."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Anthropic is betting that Fable 5 is so good that people will pay. And for some use cases, it genuinely is. But with Chinese models delivering 80-90% of the performance at 10-40% of the cost (see Story 4), and OpenAI's Sol dropping tomorrow, this pricing feels like it was set in a pre-GLM-5.2 world. The market has moved. Anthropic might not have noticed."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Score: 5/10 -- Expected, but the optics are terrible given the competitive landscape."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
