    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Key Details",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Architecture: Full-duplex -- processes input while generating output"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Natural conversation: Uses backchanneling (\"mhmm\", \"yeah\") to show attention"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Interruption handling: Users can cut in naturally, no push-to-talk"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Live translation: Real-time multilingual conversation support"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Two tiers: GPT-Live-1 (full intelligence) and GPT-Live-1-mini (faster, lighter)"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Availability: Rolling out globally to ChatGPT Plus/Pro/Team/Enterprise"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- CarPlay support: Included in the rollout"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "- Intelligence control: Users can set how \"smart\" the voice model behaves"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Source Credibility: HIGH",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Primary: OpenAI official blog post & @OpenAI tweet with demo video. Confirmed by VentureBeat, TechCrunch, MacRumors, Thurrott, 9to5Mac, SQ Magazine."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": ""
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "text": "Wolffish Review",
    "level": 3
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "I was skeptical about another voice model announcement, but the full-duplex thing is genuinely different. The old ChatGPT voice mode was like talking on a walkie-talkie -- you talk, then they talk. GPT-Live is like a phone call. The \"mhmm\" backchanneling might sound gimmicky, but anyone who's done UX research knows that conversational turn-taking cues are the difference between \"talking to a robot\" and \"talking to a person.\""
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "The CarPlay integration is a smart move -- voice AI in the car is the killer app nobody talks about. And releasing Live-1-mini alongside the full model shows OpenAI is thinking about latency-sensitive use cases, not just benchmark scores."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "The question: will it actually feel natural in practice, or is this another \"Advanced Voice Mode\" situation where the demo is amazing but the real experience is clunky? We'll know by tomorrow when the flood of user videos hits."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "text": "Score: 7.5/10 -- Smart product move, great timing. Execution TBD."
  },
